      {
        "y": 510.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 359.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "What can ordinary citizens do to reduce energy consumption1?"
      },
      {
        "y": 522.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 330.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Some simple things include using fewer power-hungry2"
      },
      {
        "y": 534.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "appliances3 around the home, monitoring4 your use of electricity and consuming5 less energy by"
      },
      {
        "y": 546.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "switching off unnecessary lights and entertainment systems that use power while on standby. Is your"
      },
      {
        "y": 558.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "car a gas-guzzler6? Think about changing to a more energy-efficient7 model. Think more about food"
      },
      {
        "y": 570.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "miles8 and buy local products, so that fuel consumption in the transporting of goods is reduced. We"
      },
      {
        "y": 582.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "can also reduce our carbon footprint9 by planning travel more carefully and cutting out unnecessary"
      },
      {
        "y": 594.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "journeys. Remember, the world’s coal, oil and gas deposits10 are finite11; one day they will run out, so"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 308.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "think now about what you can do to consume less."
      },
