      },
      {
        "y": 347.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 505.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 A new 100-kilometre metal tube has been built to bring oil from the holes in the ground for"
      },
      {
        "y": 359.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 403.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "extracting oil in the north of the country to a refinery on the coast."
      },
      {
        "y": 371.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 522.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 The power station is one that uses coal, but it will soon be replaced by a plant that uses atomic"
      },
      {
        "y": 383.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 161,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "science."
      },
      {
        "y": 395.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 343.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Fire has broken out on a drilling platform in the sea."
      },
      {
        "y": 407.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 524.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 Power from the tide or from waves could solve the energy problems of countries with extensive"
      },
      {
        "y": 419.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 514.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "coastlines. Other parts of the world may be able to use energy from the heat inside the earth."
      },
      {
        "y": 431.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 503.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 ‘Energy sources that can be renewed are important,’ the Prime Minister said. ‘We intend to"
      },
      {
        "y": 443.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
